  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8867c297-e22c-45ef-bad8-424d7b0a4f40",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Notes for Histograms + Density Distribution :-**\n",
    "\n",
    "* PHQ‑9 total shows a slightly right‑skewed unimodal curve centred on ~10, confirming the numeric summary above.\n",
    "* DPQ1–DPQ8 & DPQ10 (symptom frequency items) are heavily left‑skewed; the modal response is “0 = Not at all”, tapering to very few “3 = Nearly every day”.\n",
    "* This long‑tail behaviour is typical in population‑level mental‑health screenings and motivates a later binarisation step.\n",
    "* DPQ9 (suicidal ideation) has an extreme spike at 0 and much thinner tails at 1–3, which is epidemiologically expected but important for risk‑stratification logic.\n",
    "* Across items, variance increases with the mean, foreshadowing potential heteroskedasticity – hence the later use of Welch‐adjusted tests.\n"
   ]
  },
